[COMMENTS]
STATION,Velocity area station gauging a natural, rural catchment. GENERAL: 20m open channel with full cableway. Gravel boulder and rock control. Station added to peak flows dataset in September 2019 (WINFAP Files v8). STATION HYDROMETRY: One peak flow rating across period of record, gauged to just over 3m, with a measured flow of 135 cumecs. Flows are based on simple extrapolation beyond the highest gauging. FLOW REGIME: Natural catchment with no significant storage.
CATCHMENT,Significant arable and pasture agriculture in lower reaches with rough grazing, moorland and peat bog in the upper catchment.
Qmed Suitability,Well gauged to QMED.
Pooling Suitability,Calibration based on gauging up to 3.039m, then simple extrapolation thereafter. The flood gaugings provide some confidence in the Peak Flow data.
[END]
